From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: i2c: i2c-mt65xx: add MediaTek MT6897

The I2C controllers of the MediaTek MT6897 (Dimensity 8300) SoC work
like the MT8188 ones. In the MediaTek driver in the OnePlus MT6897
kernel, the mt6897 data has the same register offsets as the mainline
mt_i2c_regs_v3 (the slave address at 0x94, selected there by
slave_addr_ver), the same timing, auto restart and auxiliary length
handling, no dma_sync, apdma_sync and 36-bit DMA addresses. Its dma_ver
1 writes the same skip-config, async and direction-change bits to the
DMA controller as the mainline apdma_sync path does.

The MediaTek driver also has a FIFO path for short transfers, which the
mainline driver does not use for any SoC.

Add MT6897 with mediatek,mt8188-i2c as the fallback, as MT6878 and
MT6991 have.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-mt65xx.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-mt65xx.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-mt65xx.yaml
index ecd5783..47de29e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-mt65xx.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-mt65xx.yaml
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - enum:
               - mediatek,mt6878-i2c
+              - mediatek,mt6897-i2c
               - mediatek,mt6991-i2c
               - mediatek,mt8189-i2c
               - mediatek,mt8196-i2c
